# Slice 333 (the author 2026-11-09: `fn: prepared`, "в любой момент можем подставить заготовленную структуру ресиверу
# fn и это будет объявлением функции в namespace"): prepared is an ordinary Structure in code with the field name and
# the other arguments of fn; `fn: prepared` supplies them by their names, and the receiver creates the function triple
# in the namespace of this traversal, where the traversal reaches it. Its var is the written var (calls) completed by the
# own fields of the body (last), by the one constructor of every form; prepared stays as written. Slice 334 (Codex
# review of 333): `fn: other prepared` gives the same Structure to the form with a separate name -- its field name is an
# ordinary field there -- and the var of other is completed the same way (last), its counters its own.
int: k 2
prepared:
    name: triple
    args: (int: a)
    return: int
    var: (int: calls 0)
    body: (calls := calls + 1; int: last a; return: last * 3 + k)
end: prepared
fn: prepared
fn: other prepared
k := 4
int: r1 triple(5)
int: r2 triple(2)
int: c1 triple\var\calls
int: c2 triple\var\last
int: r3 other(3)
int: c3 other\var\calls
int: c4 other\var\last
